WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.200
Weekly grids, planning lists, exam lists, the room master: the files the office already keeps

2
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:15.500
Drop an edited room master: each change is shown before anything is saved

3
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.500
A real solver run on the autumn term's data

4
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.500
Hard rules held: every exception is one the planning list asked for, named and counted

5
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:26.800
The report lists each class that could not be placed, and why

6
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.100
Each comes with concrete fixes: a free room and time, and what else would move

7
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:34.400
Publish: the dialog says what is left out before anyone sees the plan

8
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.700
Published: bookings, calendars and the dashboard now follow this plan

9
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.000
When: tomorrow, a free period

10
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:43.000
Where: how many people; only rooms that are free and fit are listed

11
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.000
One tap books it; the server checks the slot first

12
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.600
The approver's inbox: open the request

13
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.600
Approve: the server re-checks the slot first

14
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.200
The requester sees it confirmed, with every decision

15
00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:01.300
Admins pick the AI provider and model for each feature, and see who used how many tokens

16
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:06.700
Guardrails keep the models on scheduling: injection and off-topic requests are refused

17
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:11.200
The operations panel: service health, metrics and the error log in one place

